WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
One morning, a child had tea before heading out.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
He tasted it and said, “Mom, this tea is bitter.”

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:23.000
“Stir it,” she said. He stirred, but it was still bitter.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Life can feel like that, too.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:43.000
We work hard for money and education, seek love, and build families—

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:53.000
yet the bitterness inside can remain.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:02.000
We keep hoping that tomorrow will be better.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Many of us know that feeling of frustration and loss.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:17.000
But the Christian message offers a different kind of hope.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:27.000
The Bible speaks of a God who was, is, and always will be.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:37.000
The One who made heaven and earth and cares about people.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:44.000
With God as our refuge, we do not have to carry life alone.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Scripture says God would come and be with us.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:04.000
“Immanuel” means “God with us”—
a name given to Jesus.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Jesus is more than a figure from history.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:29.800
Christians believe God came as a human being
to bring us salvation and be our Savior.
